      29: Text { content: "Egypt" }
      30: Text { content: ". This is the meaning of “But mingled themselves with the nations, and learned their works.” It means that if " }
      31: Text { content: "Israel" }
      32: Text { content: " are under the dominion of a certain nation, that nation controls them and they cannot retire from their dominion. Thus, they tasted sufficient flavor in that work and could not be redeemed." }
      33: EndParagraph
      34: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
      35: Text { content: "So" }
